-- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit, the system SHALL retain the submitted payload with its visit ID, author ID, and server receipt time.
-- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance result without creating another stored submission.
-- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission and leave the original submission unchanged.
-- [ ] **REC-004**: When edits derived from the same starting visit state are accepted, the system SHALL preserve both original submissions regardless of the concurrency policy's outcome.
-- [ ] **REC-005**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL indicate whether unresolved review work exists for that visit.
-- [ ] **REC-006**: When a coordinator resolves review work, the system SHALL retain the coordinator's identity and the contributing submission IDs with the resolution outcome.
+## Submission Handling
+
+- [ ] **REC-001**: When an authenticated worker submits a valid visit edit with an idempotency key, the system SHALL generate a revision_id, store the submitted visit state, author ID, and server receipt time, and return a submission acceptance response including the new revision_id and the base_revision_id the submission was tied to.
+- [ ] **REC-002**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with an identical payload, the system SHALL return the original acceptance response without creating another revision.
+- [ ] **REC-003**: When a submission repeats an accepted idempotency key with a different payload, the system SHALL reject the submission with a conflict error and leave the original submission unchanged.
+- [ ] **REC-004**: When a worker submits an edit referencing a base_revision_id, the system SHALL accept the submission even if other revisions exist for that visit, creating no automatic merge and creating no new current state.
+- [ ] **REC-005**: When a submission arrives from the same base_revision_id as an existing revision for the same visit_id, the system SHALL mark the visit as unresolved and set unresolved_flag to true.
+
+## Current-State Retrieval
+
+- [ ] **REC-010**: When a caller retrieves a visit that has exactly one submitted revision, the system SHALL return current_state as that revision, current_revision_id as that revision's ID, unresolved_flag as false, and competing_revision_ids as an empty list.
+- [ ] **REC-011**: When a caller retrieves a visit that has multiple submitted revisions with no coordinator selection, the system SHALL return unresolved_flag as true and competing_revision_ids as the full list of submitted revision IDs (excluding any previously resolved selections).
+- [ ] **REC-012**: When a caller retrieves a visit, the system SHALL include complete submission metadata with each retrieved state: author ID, base_revision_id, and server receipt time.
+
+## Resolution Operations
+
+- [ ] **REC-020**: When a coordinator selects a competing revision as the resolution for an unresolved visit, the system SHALL record the selection as an immutable resolution event containing the winning revision ID, the list of other revision IDs being superseded, the coordinator's authenticated identity, and a server timestamp.
+- [ ] **REC-021**: When a resolution event is recorded for a visit, the system SHALL set current_revision_id to the winning revision ID and unresolved_flag to false on subsequent retrievals.
+- [ ] **REC-022**: When a new submission arrives for an already-resolved visit (with a base_revision_id matching a now-superseded revision), the system SHALL treat the new submission as a fresh competing edit, mark the visit as unresolved again, and add the new revision to the competing list.
+
+## Preservation
+
+- [ ] **REC-030**: The system SHALL never discard an accepted submission. Submissions not selected by a coordinator's resolution remain queryable for audit and historical review.
